A Mobile Virtual Network Operator (MVNO) is a wireless communications services provider that does not own the radio spectrum or network infrastructure over which it provides services. Instead, MVNOs enter into business agreements with traditional Mobile Network Operators (MNOs) to purchase network capacity at wholesale rates and then sell services to consumers under their own brand. This model enables them to offer specialized service bundles, digital-first operations, and highly customer-centric solutions.
